# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# ## How the hashes in this policy are produced
#
# `script-src` and `style-src` carry SHA-256 hashes of the two inline blocks in
# the built `dist/index.html`. They are NOT hand-written, and they are not
# stable across edits - regenerating them is part of the build:
#
#     npm run website:csp      # writes the hashes into dist/_headers
#     npm run website:check    # fails if a hash does not match the build
#
# `website:check` recomputes both hashes from `dist/index.html` and compares
# them against this file. That is the check that makes a stale hash a build
# failure rather than a silently blank page.
#
# ## Why hashes and not a nonce
#
# A nonce is the stronger mechanism, but a nonce has to be fresh per request
# AND present as an attribute on the element. Cloudflare Pages serves a static
# file: `_headers` is parsed at deploy time and its values are sent verbatim.
# There is no per-request substitution, so a nonce cannot be injected into
# already-built inline markup.
#
# This was measured, not assumed. Serving the real `dist/` under the real
# headers on 1 Oct 2026 produced, in Chrome:
#
#   The source list for 'script-src' contains an invalid source: ''nonce-{RANDOM}''
#   Executing inline script violates ... 'script-src'. The action has been blocked.
#
# The page fell back to Times New Roman and 3,741 characters instead of
# Inter and 5,679 - the script never ran. `{RANDOM}` was a literal placeholder
# that no Cloudflare feature replaces. It has been removed rather than left to
# look like a working configuration.
#
# `'strict-dynamic'` is kept: it lets the hashed bundle load what it needs
# without enumerating every host.
#
# There is deliberately NO `unsafe-hashes`. It was here for four cost-bar
# widths written as `style="--bar-width: 45%"`. A nonce cannot cover a style
# attribute, and those four attributes were real violations - four "Applying
# inline style violates ... style-src" errors, with the bars rendering at 0%.
# They are now CSS custom properties declared in `styles/theme.css`, and
# main.js updates them through the CSSOM, which CSP does not govern.
#
# The page therefore has no escape hatch at all: no `unsafe-inline`, no
# `unsafe-eval`, no `unsafe-hashes`, no `on*=` handlers, no `style=`
# attributes.
#
# `scripts/gates/check-website-build.mjs` fails the build if this file goes
# missing, loses its CSP directive, regains any `unsafe-*` keyword, or if a
# hash stops matching the build.
#
# ## Two syntax rules this file obeys, both learned the hard way
#
# 1. ONE header per line, value on the SAME line as the name.
#    Cloudflare Pages parses `[name]: [value]` as a single line. The policy was
#    originally written folded across eleven lines, one directive per line, and
#    Pages silently discarded it. On 2 Oct 2026 that shipped to production and
#    the site served with NO Content-Security-Policy at all: 200 OK, correct
#    HTML, and no header. Nothing in this repository noticed, because every
#    check here reads this file, not the deployed response.
#    Confirmed by measurement: folded = header absent; one line = header served.
#
# 2. ONE `/*` block, not three.
#    Repeating the URL pattern does NOT merge blocks - each `/*` starts a new
#    one. The second and third blocks were never applied either. Verified on a
#    live preview: three blocks served only the last one's header, while a
#    single block served all of them.
#
# Cloudflare's own docs (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers)
# show one `[name]: [value]` per line under a single URL pattern, and note the
# file is parsed at deploy time and never served as an asset.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'PLACEHOLDER_SCRIPT' 'strict-dynamic'; style-src 'PLACEHOLDER_STYLE' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload